# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Every value here is read from the environment
# at runtime — nothing is baked into the build — so one image can be promoted
# across environments unchanged. In development the code degrades rather than
# crashes when a value is absent; in production a missing RECAPTCHA_SECRET_KEY
# or POSTGRES_URL makes /api/feedback refuse submissions.

# --- Assistant (/api/chat) --------------------------------------------------
MODEL_API_KEY=
OPENAI_BASE_URL=
MODEL=
# MODEL_MAX_TOKENS=4096

# --- reCAPTCHA v2 (/api/feedback) -------------------------------------------
# Both are read at runtime, so the same built image works in any environment.
# The site key reaches the browser as a prop rendered by /feedback, not as a
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* value baked into the client bundle at build time.
# Set both together: without the site key the checkbox never renders, and in
# production a missing secret makes the API refuse submissions outright rather
# than accept them unverified.
RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=
RECAPTCHA_SECRET_KEY=

# --- Postgres: system of record for feedback submissions --------------------
# URL may carry the credentials inline; when it does, leave USER/PASSWORD
# blank. When both are set, USER/PASSWORD win over anything in the URL.
POSTGRES_URL=postgres://db-host.example.com:5432/jaia
POSTGRES_USER=
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# TLS: disable | no-verify | verify-full. Defaults to no-verify for a remote
# host and disable for localhost.
# POSTGRES_SSL=
# POSTGRES_POOL_MAX=3
